{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793176199,"nonce":"s3f8/+WghpEBs2t3aaTrbbyAu+8=","title":"Resolve browser host assets relative to their module","message":"The page host currently creates thread/program/display workers relative to the containing document and resolves dynamic native agent imports against location.href. An application using web/ashui-host.mjs from a nested assets directory consequently loads some files next to the page and others next to the bundle. RayDE's landing page had to patch generated output manually. Resolve the program, workers and native agent shims through import.meta.url so regenerated builds retain a consistent bundle-relative contract. Exercise a page whose canvas and metadata are at a different path from the host, plus the standalone generated page.\n\nBackport on rayde-browser-input to keep RayDE's existing renderer/compiler pin unchanged apart from this host fix. Related RayDE landing tracker 66e2d7d.","files":null}]}